id: heavy-suppression
name: Heavy Suppression
type: form
subtype: alternate
racial: Arcosian
prerequisites: Emperor Mutation Trait
line: metamorphosis
stage: 1
tier: 2+
stress: 12
aspects: Enhanced Save (Corporeal/Impulsive), Draining (LV1), Power High (LV1)
bonuses: AG +1(T), FO +1(T), TE +1(T), IN +1(T), MA +1(T)
# The Metamorphosis Forms text box: for this Stage, a Size Category, S Evolution Traits, a Tail Attack choice and a Survivor Option -
# chosen on its row, had while in it (transformations.mjs rowChoicesOf, syncWhileIn; its script below).
choice1: size | Size | small=Small; medium=Medium; large=Large
choice2: tail | Tail Attack | none=None; elongated=Elongated; multiple=Multiple; spiked=Spiked; heavy=Heavy
choice3: survivor | Survivor | dense-plating=Dense Plating; sleek-plating=Sleek Plating; power-plating=Power Plating; combat-plating=Combat Plating
choice4: evolution1 | Evolution Trait | @other:evolution
# The Tail Attack Maneuver's choice and Survivor's Option replaced while in this Stage, put back on leaving it.
tailWhileIn: $row.tail
optionWhileIn: survivor = $row.survivor
description: >
  The overflowing power within your body is so great that- at least, at first- even you cannot control it. You must reinforce your body with layers upon layers of bio-armor, creating transformations to suppress your full power. Even with your power concealed in this way, you still remain among the strongest fighters in the universe, and when push comes to shove, you can unleash your full power, even if only for a moment.
text: >
  The overflowing power within your body is so great that- at least, at first- even you cannot control it. You must reinforce your body with layers upon layers of bio-armor, creating transformations to suppress your full power. Even with your power concealed in this way, you still remain among the strongest fighters in the universe, and when push comes to shove, you can unleash your full power, even if only for a moment.

  **Heavy Suppression** — Racial Requirement: Arcosian / Form / Alternate / Prerequisite(s): Emperor Mutation Trait / Line: Metamorphosis / Stage: 1 / Stress Test Requirement: 12 / Tier of Power Requirement. 2+
  Aspects: Enhanced Save (Corporeal/Impulsive), Draining (LV1), Power High (LV1)
  AG +1(T) · FO +1(T) · TE +1(T) · SC – · IN +1(T) · MA +1(T) · PE –

  Overwhelming Strike: Any worm that dares to raise a hand against you will find that your brutality and power can pierce even the toughest hides.
  (1)-[Passive]: While you are in the Healthy Health Threshold, increase the Damage Category of all of your Signature Techniques by 1 Category.
  (2)-[Passive]: If you are above the Injured Health Threshold, increase the Wound Rolls of your Signature Techniques by x(T), where x is equal to their Damage Category.
  (3)-[Triggered/Transform, 1/Round]: Enter the Superior State until the start of your next turn.

  Overwhelming Mutant: As you shed layers of suppression like dead scales, your peerless power shines brighter, overwhelming any foe.
  (1)-[Passive]: While you possess 2+ stacks of Power, increase your Wound Rolls and Soak Value by 1/2 of S(T).
  (2)-[Triggered/Power]: You may spend 2 stacks of Overwhelm to gain an additional stack of Power from this use of the Power Up Maneuver.
  (3)-[Triggered, 1/Encounter]: At the end of your turn, spend all stacks of Overwhelm to regain 3(bT) Life Points for each stack spent.
  (4)-[Triggered, 1/Encounter]: At the end of your turn, do not trigger the 2nd effect of Overwhelming Fighter.

  MASTERY TRAIT — Overwhelming Transformation: Even shedding a single layer of your suppression is enough to overwhelm most enemies.
  (1)-[Permanent]: This Transformation loses the Draining and Power High Aspects and gains the Natural (LV2) Aspect.
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase the Apparel Bonus of your Plating by 1(T).
  (3)-[Triggered/Transform, Triggered/Start of Turn]: Gain a stack of Overwhelm.

---

# The Metamorphosis Forms text box: what was chosen for this Stage, on its row, while in it. An Evolved Stage on it uses these (it has
# none of its own; this Stage stays in use beneath it).

# "A Size Category between Small and Large. This replaces your base Size Category while you are in that Stage."
[passive]
if ($is.size.small == 1) {
    allow size.base.small;
}
if ($is.size.medium == 1) {
    allow size.base.medium;
}
if ($is.size.large == 1) {
    allow size.base.large;
}
